{"title":"Career roadmap — CSR Executive","role":"CSR Executive","summary":"A CSR Executive supports corporate social responsibility programmes by identifying social needs, coordinating projects with NGOs and communities, tracking budgets and activities, measuring impact, preparing reports and ensuring that CSR initiatives align with organisational objectives and applicable regulations.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Rural Development / Women's Studies / Gender Studies"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a graduate in Rural Development, Women's Studies or Gender Studies, CSR can be a strong career because the academic background provides understanding of communities, inequality, livelihoods, gender, social development and inclusion."},{"type":"flow","items":["The strongest profile combines social-sector knowledge","project management","CSR compliance","impact measurement","corporate communication."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"CSR roles in India can involve specific legal, governance and reporting requirements under applicable corporate regulations. A CSR Executive should learn the current rules relevant to the organisation rather than relying on outdated compliance checklists."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build social-development knowledge, CSR fundamentals, project coordination, M&E and corporate communication"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in CSR programme management, ESG, rural development, gender inclusion, education, healthcare or livelihoods"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress to CSR Manager, Social Impact Manager, CSR Partnerships Lead or ESG/Impact Specialist"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead large CSR portfolios, corporate foundations, social-impact str